title: '[eth-rpc]: add resumable block sync and improve CLI arguments'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: "### Resumable block sync\n- New block_sync module syncs backward from\
    \ the latest finalized block to the first EVM block, with crash-safe checkpoint\
    \ tracking via a sync_state SQLite table.\n- On restart, fills only the top gap\
    \ (new blocks) and bottom gap (remaining backfill) without re-syncing completed\
    \ ranges.\n- Auto-discovers and persists `evm_first_block` \u2014 the lowest block\
    \ with EVM support on the chain.\n- Chain identity verification: Store genesis\
    \ hash in sync_state and validate on startup; detect stale boundaries after reorgs.\n\
    \n### CLI rework\n- Replace --database-url with --database-name + --base-path\n\
    - Replace --index-last-n-blocks with --sync (enables backward block sync, requires\
    \ persistent DB)\n- Replace --cache-size with --prune (uses an in-memory database\
    \ keeping only the latest N blocks)"
crates:
- name: pallet-revive-eth-rpc
  bump: minor
